From 3311db27d26d58558f2380d22fcc3af76be84532 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 02:00:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] Per-client WebSocket presence and focus tracking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each TUI process opens one long-lived WebSocket on /presence for the
life of the TUI. The connection itself is the presence beacon — when
it closes (clean exit, SIGINT, kill, network drop), the WebSocket
protocol's CLOSE frame triggers `onClose` on the server synchronously
and the entry is removed from `_clients`.

The protocol on /presence is bidirectional and carries presence state
end-to-end on a single channel:

  client → server: { "type": "focus",         "sessionID": "ses_..." | null }
  server → client: { "type": "live-sessions", "sessions":  string[] }

Server-side `_clients` is module-scoped (cross-directory by
construction). `_publishChange` does a fan-out send over every
connected WS rather than routing through `Bus.publish`. Bus events are
per-instance (per-directory) — using them for presence silently
dropped cross-worktree deliveries, so the pill desynced for the
common multi-worktree workflow. Broadcasting on the WS itself, where
the cross-directory map already lives, removes the inconsistency.

The TUI side lives in a small dedicated module
(`cli/cmd/tui/context/presence-client.ts`) that owns the WS lifecycle,
reconnect with backoff, and `currentFocus` tracking. Every `onopen`
(initial AND reconnect) re-sends `currentFocus`, so transient drops
and daemon restarts self-correct without external nudging.
`sdk.tsx` synthesizes `session.live.changed` events from incoming
broadcasts so the footer plugin's `api.event.on("session.live.changed", ...)`
contract is preserved unchanged.

Footer pills:
  ● N sessions  — global, deduplicated set of focused sessionIDs
  ● N subagents — per-TUI count of `session.children(focused)`
                  (intentionally not routed through this channel)

Replaces an 11-patch SSE iteration: native Bun.serve + uSockets
EPOLLRDHUP delivers synchronous WebSocket close events that the
@hono/node-server compat layer batched behind unrelated I/O.

Tests: 14 in total. Server-side suite (presence.test.ts) exercises
the `_clients` map with real Bun.serve + real WebSocket clients; the
`broadcast crosses directories` test pins the regression that
motivated removing Bus.publish. Client-side suite
(presence-client.test.ts) exercises the TUI module end-to-end against
a real Bun.serve, including a daemon-restart scenario where a fresh
server comes up on the same port and the client must self-restore
its currentFocus.
